From: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: remove netsys v1 restriction for
 small frag check

All TX DMAs across all Netsys versions have a hardware limitation that
SDL must not be less than 16, so the Netsys version check has to be
removed.

Without this patch, the TX DMA may behave unexpectedly when processing
fragments shorter than 16 bytes.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/241d864218630c9cb380a3657c89f8fc3bdc3434/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-eth-56-mtk_eth_soc-remove-netsys-v1-restriction-for-small-frag-check.patch
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2119,7 +2119,7 @@ static bool mtk_skb_has_small_frag(struc
 static bool mtk_skb_valid_gso(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			      unsigned int header_len)
 {
-	if (mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) && mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb))
+	if (mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb))
 		return false;
 
 	if (!(skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_type & SKB_GSO_FRAGLIST))
@@ -2201,8 +2201,7 @@ static netdev_tx_t mtk_start_xmit(struct
 
 send:
 	skb_list_walk_safe(skb, skb, next) {
-		if ((mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) &&
-		     mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
+		if ((mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
 		    mtk_tx_map(skb, dev, tx_num, ring, gso, header_len) < 0) {
 				stats->tx_dropped++;
 				dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
